<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram id="p_01_roles_and_the_boundary" name="01-roles-and-the-boundary"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="771" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="The reasoner proposes, only the coordinator invokes: one shared kernel owns every authority, and each experience owns only its story, reached through one small effect vocabulary" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="visitor" value="VISITOR&#10;at a public&#10;demo stand" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="190" width="110" height="90" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="reasoner" value="THE REASONER&#10;(a realtime speech-to-speech LLM session)&#10;&#10;OWNS everything said inside a phase: wording, tone, empathy, small detours&#10;&#10;MAY propose a physical act, as a typed intent from a closed list (its one tool)&#10;&#10;GETS a small per-phase context, e.g. 'this is the greeting; a wave is available'. It is never told it is bounded.&#10;&#10;RETURNS a turn result: typed intent + terminal speech status&#10;&#10;CHAT = bounded turns: 3 turns [I1] x 8 s [I2] = 24 s [calc] inside a 60 s session bound [I3]; one speech-output lease per turn" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="170" y="80" width="250" height="310" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="coord" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="500" y="72" width="480" height="362" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="coord_t" value="THE COORDINATOR = kernel + the selected experience. Deterministic code, one worker, one authoritative transition at a time. Only it invokes anything." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="510" y="76" width="460" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="kernel" value="COORDINATOR KERNEL  (shared by every experience)&#10;&#10;owns: event admission and ordering | correlation | participant authority (who the visitor is) | safety preemption | command authority, leases and the visitor-audio permit | timer mechanics | cleanup and the proof that every store is clean | the lifecycle | evidence" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="515" y="116" width="450" height="130" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="effects" value="EFFECT VOCABULARY - the only way out:&#10;invoke primitive | cancel primitive | start / cancel timer | request completion cleanup | report to operator" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="603" y="262" width="280" height="56" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="exper" value="SELECTED EXPERIENCE  (one per coordinator process)&#10;pure reducer: (local state, read-only envelope, event) -&gt; (next local state, ordered effects)&#10;owns: its local story state, transition matrix, story invariants, and its own timeout, retry and participant POLICY choices" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="515" y="334" width="450" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pcat" value="PRIMITIVE CATALOG (out)&#10;every behaviour, speech act, gaze request and session service an experience may invoke" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1010" y="116" width="240" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="icat" value="INPUT CATALOG (in)&#10;every input: ingress kind, payload, correlation, privacy, replay policy" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1010" y="200" width="240" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="adapt" value="PER-TARGET CONTRACTS&#10;adapters (for primitives) and producers (for inputs), one per named target" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1010" y="290" width="240" height="62" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tgt" value="TARGETS&#10;simulation | physical robot" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1010" y="374" width="240" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="never" value="WHAT EACH SIDE MAY NEVER DO&#10;An experience cannot call the robot middleware, the behaviour library, the browser, a model, the clock, the file system or the network (A0).&#10;The reasoner has no motion tool; its tool, context and ability sets are empty and it gets no camera images; its output never selects an experience, a state, a primitive or a command (A1, B6)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="448" width="600" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="shrink" value="WHAT THE KERNEL BUYS&#10;A single-experience coordinator named story actions directly: an effect list of about 30 kinds [I4]. The kernel replaces it with the handful of generic effects above plus the two catalogs. A new experience that recombines registered parts is an authoring task, with no kernel change (A0)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="650" y="448" width="600" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="alts" value="REJECTED ALTERNATIVES (A0):  one coordinator process per experience (safety and cleanup diverge)  |  one large reducer with configuration branches (one matrix for unrelated stories)  |  a workflow language (validation becomes an interpreter)  |  runtime plug-ins (weakens pinning and review)  |  an LLM that orchestrates at run time (model output cannot own safety, cleanup, identity or physical authority)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="532" width="1220" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  purple = the reasoner  |  amber = the kernel and its authority  |  green = the experience (story only)  |  blue = catalogs, per-target contracts, targets  |  red = never allowed  |  dashed frame = the coordinator. Thick arrows = the path of one proposed act." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="592" width="1220" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Mechanisms: this kit's notes/ (named per line below) and glossary.md. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown: [Pn] = public (cited); [In] = illustrative (a round design parameter that keeps the design's relations; never a measurement of any system); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/A0-one-experience-versus-many.md (kernel concerns, rejected alternatives, vocabulary shrink); A1-the-reasoner-and-the-coordinator.md (ownership table, proposal path); B1 (reducer signature); B3-the-effect-vocabulary.md (effect table); B5 (catalogs, targets); B6-conversation-and-model-boundaries.md (capability and output boundaries, bounded turns). [calc]: 24 s = 3 turns x 8 s; it fits inside the 60 s session bound.&#10;[I1] chat_turns_illustrative = 3 turns. illustrative: design parameter; bounded number of conversation turns in the example chat experience&#10;[I2] chat_turn_budget_s_illustrative = 8 s. illustrative: design parameter; per-turn time budget for one conversation turn&#10;[I3] chat_session_bound_s_illustrative = 60 s. illustrative: design parameter; upper bound on one kernel-owned conversation session&#10;[I4] old_effect_kinds_illustrative = 30 effect kinds. illustrative order of magnitude of a story-specific effect vocabulary in a single-experience coordinator, before the generic vocabulary replaced it" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="644" width="1220" height="111" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="speech" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.3;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.44193548387096776;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="visitor" target="reasoner"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="speech" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=0;exitY=0.5580645161290323;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.7;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="reasoner" target="visitor"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="typed intent&#10;(a proposal,&#10;never a command)" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.25806451612903225;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3384615384615385;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="reasoner" target="kernel"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="phase context;&#10;'not now'" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;exitX=0;exitY=0.8;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.45161290322580644;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="kernel" target="reasoner"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="admitted,&#10;ordered event" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.06666666666666667;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.06666666666666667;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="kernel" target="exper"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge5" value="effects&#10;(validated&#10;before commit)" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.9333333333333333;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.9333333333333333;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="exper" target="kernel"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge6" value="dispatch&#10;(after commit)" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.26153846153846155;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.4857142857142857;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="kernel" target="pcat"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge7" value="events" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0;exitY=0.35714285714285715;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.8384615384615385;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="icat" target="kernel"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge8" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pcat" target="adapt"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1266" y="151" /><mxPoint x="1266" y="321" /></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge9" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=0.3;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.3;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="adapt" target="icat"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge10" value="commands out, observations in" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="adapt" target="tgt"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_02_one_event_path" name="02-one-event-path"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="673" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="One event, one path: the kernel orders, admits and intercepts every input first; the reducer sees only what is left, and nothing is sent until one snapshot is committed" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s0" value="perception" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="84" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s1" value="reasoner turn results" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="116" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s2" value="motion-layer outcomes" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="148" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s3" value="timers" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="180" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s4" value="operator" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="212" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s5" value="simulation" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="244" width="150" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="srch" value="INPUTS -&gt; typed events" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="64" width="150" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="queue" value="1  ONE BOUNDED PRIORITY QUEUE, ONE WORKER&#10;&#10;priority order:&#10;1 safety  &gt;  2 reset  &gt;  3 operator control  &gt;  4 correlated command outcomes  &gt;  5 observations&#10;&#10;inside one priority, a total order from: normalised observation time -&gt; source rank -&gt; source sequence -&gt; event ID (Lamport 1978: a deterministic tie-break yields one order every replay agrees on)&#10;&#10;replay uses the recorded accepted order" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="215" y="74" width="300" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="admit" value="2  ADMISSION  (checks the event context: source, sequence, times, clock domain, epoch, uncertainty, session, generation, command)&#10;&#10;REJECTED, never reaching the reducer:&#10;- stale, duplicate, wrong generation, wrong session, wrong command&#10;- an outcome for a command that is not pending&#10;- age or timestamp uncertainty over its bound&#10;- a participant-bound input whose track is not the current participant track&#10;- a source not admitted for this target (B5: rejected before queue insertion)&#10;&#10;rejected, NOT deferred: queueing would let one visitor's content reach the next" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="545" y="74" width="340" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="icpt" value="3  INTERCEPTION  (the kernel handles these itself)&#10;&#10;safety and reset | readiness assessment, refresh, loss | start and yield of the idle 'ready' behaviour | visitor-audio permit issue, revoke, refusal | runtime faults and queue overflow | operator abort | participant retirement needing cleanup | cleanup acknowledgements and the cleanup deadline | the startup proof that every store is clean&#10;&#10;No experience may override, delay or reject any of them. The kernel then derives the TENTATIVE envelope." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="915" y="74" width="335" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="red" value="4  REDUCER (the experience)&#10;pure: (local state, read-only envelope, event) -&gt; (next local state, ordered effects)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="val" value="5  VALIDATE, in order:&#10;kernel invariants (cannot be waived) -&gt; story invariants -&gt; every effect" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="236" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ids" value="6  DERIVE COMMAND IDs&#10;deterministically, so a re-dispatch is idempotent" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="442" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="mat" value="7  MATERIALISE commands and verify the tentative snapshot" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="648" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cmt" value="8  COMMIT ONE SNAPSHOT&#10;envelope + local state + pending commands + leases + timers" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=3;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="854" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dsp" value="9  DISPATCH&#10;in effect order, through the catalog to the per-target adapters" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="320" width="190" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="fail_pre" value="Any failure in steps 4-7: NOTHING is committed and NOTHING is dispatched. A rejected event in step 2 never reaches the reducer, so no experience can act on it by mistake." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="418" width="808" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="outbox" value="Transactional outbox: state and intent are recorded together, then sent; a fast completion can never arrive before the state that records its command." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="854" y="418" width="190" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="fail_post" value="A dispatcher failure AFTER commit takes the correlated failure path; it never erases or invents command state." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="418" width="190" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="safety" value="Safety sorts first and is still typed and admitted. Preemption is proven from every local state of every registered experience (C2). Software preemption is additive: the guaranteed stop is a hardware relay in the emergency-stop loop (B4)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="470" width="808" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  amber = kernel-owned steps  |  green = the one step the experience owns  |  blue = inputs and dispatch targets  |  red = what failure means  |  thick border = the commit point. One worker processes one event at a time: a public stand produces few events per second, so replayability, not throughput, is the constraint." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="528" width="1220" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Mechanisms: this kit's notes/ (named per line below) and glossary.md. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown: [Pn] = public (cited); [In] = illustrative (a round design parameter that keeps the design's relations; never a measurement of any system); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/B4-kernel-interception-and-arbitration.md (intercepted classes, one ordered queue, priority and tie-break, admission rejections, rejection not deferral, single worker, hardware stop); B3-the-effect-vocabulary.md (atomic preparation and dispatch steps, transactional outbox, deterministic command IDs); B5 (target-scoped producer admission); C2 (preemption from every local state). Public: Lamport, 'Time, clocks, and the ordering of events in a distributed system', Communications 21(7), 1978; Richardson, 'Pattern: Transactional outbox', microservices.io. Step numbers on this page are a drawing order, not the numbering in the notes. This page carries no numeric design parameter." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="582" width="1220" height="75" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.115;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s0" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.275;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s1" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.435;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s2" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.595;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.755;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s4" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge5" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.915;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s5" target="queue"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge6" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="queue" target="admit"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge7" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="admit" target="icpt"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge8" value="delegate only what is left" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="icpt" target="red"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1082" y="297" /><mxPoint x="125" y="297" /></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge9" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="red" target="val"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge10" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="val" target="ids"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge11" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ids" target="mat"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge12" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="mat" target="cmt"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge13" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="cmt" target="dsp"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_03_state_ownership" name="03-state-ownership"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="753" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="The kernel owns the envelope; each experience owns only an opaque local story that runs inside the one shared phase 'in story', and cannot write anything around it" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="env" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="70" width="820" height="440" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="env_t" value="THE KERNEL ENVELOPE  (kernel-owned; an experience reads it through a read-only view)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="42" y="74" width="796" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="fields" value="execution mode and lifecycle phase | deployment generation and session ID | provisional visitor candidate, active participant binding, reattach / departure / retirement state | capability health | visitor-audio permit (listening, per session) and speech-output lease (speaking, per turn), kept apart | action leases and per-invocation claims, open intervals, pending cancellations | timers, deadlines, pending commands | cleanup, safety, stop and recovery state | selected experience ID + revision | the opaque local state" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="98" width="790" height="74" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph_t" value="LIFECYCLE PHASE - one closed set shared by every experience (listed in the order of note B2)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="180" width="790" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph0" value="not ready" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="200" width="90" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph1" value="ready" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="144" y="200" width="90" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph2" value="selecting" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="243" y="200" width="90" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph3" value="in story" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="342" y="200" width="90" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph4" value="cleanup" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="441" y="200" width="90" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph5" value="safe cleanup" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="540" y="200" width="90" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph6" value="stopped" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="639" y="200" width="90" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ph7" value="recovery" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="738" y="200" width="90" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="story" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="286" width="790" height="210" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="story_t" value="LOCAL STORY STATE - private to the selected experience, opaque to the kernel, valid only in 'in story'. Example: the wave experience, story greet -&gt; await_wave -&gt; wave (B1)." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="57" y="290" width="770" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="greet" value="greet&#10;(chapter)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="352" width="140" height="54" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="await" value="await_wave&#10;starts a 10 s gesture-wait timer [I1]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="352" width="200" height="54" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="wave" value="wave&#10;(timer cancelled)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="640" y="352" width="170" height="54" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="gno" value="gesture_not_observed&#10;(terminal local state)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="438" width="200" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="gno_n" value="Its only effect: 'request completion cleanup'. A visitor-gesture input from any OTHER track is rejected at admission and never reaches this reducer (B4)." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="510" y="434" width="310" height="60" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="recov" value="RECOVERY is kernel-owned: unresolved claims stay in evidence and visitor admission stays off. Only explicit operator recovery, or a clean restart that proves the old authority cannot act, leaves it. The first coordinator treated this timeout as a clean stop; the kernel design corrects that (B2)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="525" width="820" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="auth" value="PARTICIPANT AUTHORITY - kernel&#10;selects the candidate, ties a handshake to a track, authorises lock, retarget, reattach and departure, retires the participant, and passes the reducer a typed decision: provisional | locked | retargeted | reattached | departed.&#10;Current participant track = active binding's track, else the candidate's; none before selection or after retirement. Invariant, independent of any story state: never a candidate AND an active participant." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="70" width="380" height="150" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pol" value="PARTICIPANT POLICY - experience&#10;only its story response plus typed options the kernel exposes, e.g. 'lock the participant when the handshake times out: yes / no'. A new lock rule or grace is a kernel change and a safety review." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="228" width="380" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="vals" value="AFTER EVERY REDUCTION, in order: 1 kernel invariants on the tentative envelope (cannot be waived) -&gt; 2 story validator (reads the envelope view, cannot change it). A failure commits nothing." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="308" width="380" height="62" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="contract" value="LOCAL STATE CONTRACT: schema version | required state_name | deep immutability (scalars, enums, tuples, frozen records; no lists, maps, sets, callables) | one kernel-owned canonical encoding | equality = equal encodings. The simulation, browser and gateway may branch only on the kernel phase and on projector values, never on a local state name." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="378" width="380" height="98" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="prof" value="TWO LEVELS OF PROFILE: the experience PROFILE (content-addressed) pins target, images, config and ABI digests, accepted inputs and primitives, catalog policy, readiness, cleanup, evidence and acceptance, and exactly one definition. The DEFINITION selects only story logic, so a story never picks its own privileges." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="484" width="380" height="98" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  amber = kernel-owned  |  green = experience-owned  |  red = recovery  |  blue = deployment profile  |  dashed amber frame = the envelope, dashed green frame = the opaque story inside 'in story'. Only the transitions the notes state are drawn between phases; the others are not." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="596" width="1220" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Mechanisms: this kit's notes/ (named per line below) and glossary.md. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown: [Pn] = public (cited); [In] = illustrative (a round design parameter that keeps the design's relations; never a measurement of any system); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/B2-state-ownership.md (envelope fields, lifecycle phases, two validators, participant authority vs policy, current participant track, local state contract, cleanup failure to recovery, two profile levels); B1-experiences-as-reducers.md (the wave example); B4 (admission of participant-bound inputs). Public: Harel, 'Statecharts', Science of Computer Programming 8(3), 1987 (a story nested inside one lifecycle state).&#10;[I1] gesture_wait_timeout_s_illustrative = 10 s. illustrative: design parameter; experience-policy timer for the 'await wave' local state of the example wave experience&#10;[I2] cleanup_ack_timeout_ms_illustrative = 10 000 ms. illustrative: design parameter; kernel cleanup acknowledgement deadline. Every settle bound must be strictly shorter" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="650" width="1220" height="87" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="greet" target="await"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="gesture = wave from the&#10;current participant track" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="await" target="wave"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="timer expiry" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="await" target="gno"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;dashed=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.43291139240506327;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ph3" target="story"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ph3" target="ph4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge5" value="cleanup deadline 10 000 ms [I2] passes without quiescence proof" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ph4" target="ph7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="486" y="262" /><mxPoint x="783" y="262" /></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_04_resource_claims" name="04-resource-claims"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="802" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="Resource claims decide what may overlap: one physical action, one gaze lease and one conversation turn can run together, but two physical actions never can, because each needs the one action slot" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="hk" value="contract kind  \  resource" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="70" width="170" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h0" value="action slot" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="200" y="70" width="118" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h1" value="body" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="318" y="70" width="118" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h2" value="head" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="436" y="70" width="118" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h3" value="gaze" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="554" y="70" width="118" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h4" value="audio out" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="672" y="70" width="118" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h5" value="listening" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="790" y="70" width="118" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="k0" value="PHYSICAL ACTION&#10;wave, expression, handshake, canned robot TTS, composites" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="110" width="170" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c00" value="ALWAYS&#10;exclusive" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="200" y="110" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c01" value="optional" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;dashed=1;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="318" y="110" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c02" value="optional;&#10;never with gaze" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;dashed=1;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="436" y="110" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c03" value="optional;&#10;never with head" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;dashed=1;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="554" y="110" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c04" value="optional" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;dashed=1;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="672" y="110" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="k1" value="GAZE LEASE&#10;set / clear a gaze target; priority derived from the gaze mode" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="176" width="170" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c10" value="-" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="200" y="176" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c11" value="-" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="318" y="176" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c12" value="-" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="436" y="176" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c13" value="EXACTLY this,&#10;exclusive" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="554" y="176" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c14" value="-" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="672" y="176" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="k2" value="SESSION SERVICE&#10;conversation turn, enrolment, gift offer, greeting, operator alert" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="242" width="170" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c20" value="-" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="200" y="242" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c21" value="-" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="318" y="242" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c22" value="-" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="436" y="242" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c23" value="-" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="554" y="242" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c24" value="nothing, or&#10;exclusive via an&#10;output lease" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="672" y="242" width="118" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="listen" value="NOT CLAIMABLE&#10;listening is the kernel's visitor-audio permit, not a resource" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="790" y="110" width="118" height="198" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rules" value="WHAT FOLLOWS (B3)&#10;- Every physical action claims the one action slot, so two physical actions never run at once.&#10;- Concurrency exists only BETWEEN kinds: one physical action + one gaze lease + one conversation turn.&#10;- Head and gaze drive the same actuators: no primitive claims both; an exclusive-head primitive is refused while a gaze lease is active.&#10;- Conversation speech (session service on an output lease) may overlap a wave; canned robot TTS cannot, it occupies the slot. A line + gesture is ONE composite primitive." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="928" y="70" width="322" height="238" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="conf" value="CONFLICT MATRIX (closed; no primitive or experience may override it, B4):  action slot - an equal-or-lower priority request is deferred, a higher one preempts and waits for the old command's terminal cancellation  |  gaze - refuses lower priority, replaces at equal or higher after the prior clear succeeds  |  audio out - a conflict is refused  |  safety priority is reserved for the kernel" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="322" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tl_t" value="THE SHOWCASE SCENARIO (C2), with the conservative first wave primitive (slot + body + head, all exclusive, no audio). Order only: the notes give no durations, so bar lengths are a drawing choice." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="382" width="1220" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lane_gaze" value="gaze (gaze lease)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="452" width="200" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="track_gaze" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=0.8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="238" y="452" width="1012" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lane_slot" value="action slot + body + head (wave)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="506" width="200" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="track_slot" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=0.8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="238" y="506" width="1012" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lane_aud" value="audio out (output lease per turn)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="560" width="200" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="track_aud" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=0.8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="238" y="560" width="1012" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g1" value="participant gaze" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="270" y="458" width="300" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g2" value="gaze reacquired" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="458" width="150" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="w1" value="wave" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="720" y="512" width="150" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="a1" value="speech turn" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="410" y="566" width="150" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="a2" value="speech turn" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="690" y="566" width="160" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st0" value="1 participant gaze acquired" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="202" y="418" width="136" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st1" value="2 brokered speech overlaps gaze" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="352" y="418" width="136" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st2" value="3 positive gaze clear (ack)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="502" y="418" width="136" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st3" value="4 brokered speech overlaps the wave" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="652" y="418" width="136" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st4" value="5 authoritative wave completion" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="802" y="418" width="136" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st5" value="6 correlated gaze reacquisition" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="952" y="418" width="136" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st6" value="7 cleanup: no retained claim" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1102" y="418" width="136" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="gap" value="Between 3 and 4 the gaze lease is cleared WITH acknowledgement before the wave starts: the wave claims the head exclusively. A lighter arm-only wave would be a later catalog revision with its own scenario (B3)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="614" width="600" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="proof" value="The video only illustrates the overlaps. The proof is the held intervals in the evidence (acquired -&gt; released per invocation), read from evidence fields, never inferred from presentation events (C2)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="650" y="614" width="600" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  matrix - solid amber = claim always held (exclusive) | dashed light amber = optional claim | white '-' = never claimed | red = not a resource.  Timeline - amber = gaze lease, green = physical action, purple = conversation turn; dashed verticals = the seven showcase steps in order." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="670" width="1220" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Mechanisms: this kit's notes/ (named per line below) and glossary.md. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown: [Pn] = public (cited); [In] = illustrative (a round design parameter that keeps the design's relations; never a measurement of any system); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/B3-the-effect-vocabulary.md (contract kinds, resources and permitted claims, action slot, head vs gaze, speech vs canned TTS, composite primitives, conservative first wave claims); B4-kernel-interception-and-arbitration.md (closed conflict matrix); C2-the-conformance-ladder.md (showcase scenario order, held intervals, 'the video illustrates, the evidence proves'). This page carries no numeric design parameter." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="724" width="1220" height="62" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="line0" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="270" y="446" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="270" y="604" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line1" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="420" y="446" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="420" y="604" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line2" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="570" y="446" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="570" y="604" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line3" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="720" y="446" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="720" y="604" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line4" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="870" y="446" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="870" y="604" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line5" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1020" y="446" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1020" y="604" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line6" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1170" y="446" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1170" y="604" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_05_cancellation_proof" name="05-cancellation-proof"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="777" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="Cancelling is not releasing: claims are kept until positive quiescence proof, and every settle bound (1500 ms [I1]) sits inside the catalog ceiling and well inside the cleanup deadline (illustrative values)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="scale_t" value="TO SCALE (one axis, 94 px per second): the three bounds a cancellation lives inside" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="66" width="1220" height="22" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b_st_l" value="target settle bound 1500 ms [I1]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="96" width="254" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b_st" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="96" width="141" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b_ce_l" value="catalog-wide ceiling 2000 ms [I2]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="130" width="254" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b_ce" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="130" width="188" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b_ck_l" value="cleanup acknowledgement deadline 10 000 ms [I3]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="164" width="254" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b_ck" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="164" width="940" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk0" value="0 s" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="260" y="208" width="60" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk2000" value="2 s" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="448" y="208" width="60" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk4000" value="4 s" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="636" y="208" width="60" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk6000" value="6 s" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="824" y="208" width="60" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk8000" value="8 s" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1012" y="208" width="60" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk10000" value="10 s" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1200" y="208" width="60" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rel" value="Relation the design relies on: settle bound &lt;= ceiling &lt; cleanup deadline. Settle deadline = the EARLIER of (request time + settle bound) and any active cleanup deadline, so a cancellation never extends cleanup." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="498" y="98" width="560" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cancel" value="CANCEL PRIMITIVE&#10;targets the original invocation (no separate 'stop' primitive); idempotent" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="302" width="190" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="settle" value="SETTLING&#10;every claim still held; the adapter must produce quiescence proof" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="302" width="220" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="q1" value="positive proof before the settle deadline?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="500" y="302" width="200" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rel1" value="RELEASE ALL the invocation's claims, at once" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="740" y="252" width="250" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="forced" value="FORCED CLEANUP, reason 'cancellation stuck': keep every claim, refuse conflicting work" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="740" y="352" width="250" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="q2" value="quiescence proved before the cleanup deadline?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="352" width="230" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rel2" value="release, normal cleanup completes" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="252" width="230" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="recov" value="RECOVERY (B2): claims stay in evidence, admission off, until operator recovery or a proven clean restart" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="452" width="230" height="64" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="proof" value="WHAT COUNTS AS PROOF (each completion contract defines it)&#10;- physical action: terminal, and no longer holds the action slot&#10;- gaze lease: the gaze clear is acknowledged&#10;- speech stream: stopped or completed, AND its stop acknowledgement succeeded" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="452" width="470" height="76" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="notproof" value="WHAT IS NOT PROOF&#10;lease expiry | readiness loss | adapter removal | a transport disconnect.&#10;Lease expiry only stops further forwarding of audio; the claim stays held until the stream proves it stopped." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="520" y="452" width="470" height="76" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="revoke" value="KERNEL REVOCATIONS ARE UNCONDITIONAL: safety and reset, readiness loss, participant departure, cleanup and generation change cancel every primitive on every target. A catalog entry may add STRICTER revokers; it cannot remove or reorder these (B3)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="540" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  bar lengths are to scale (one shared axis)  |  green = the experience's request and the clean exits  |  amber = kernel-held settlement  |  red = deadlines, non-proof, recovery  |  white = the kernel's checks." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="596" width="1220" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Mechanisms: this kit's notes/ (named per line below) and glossary.md. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown: [Pn] = public (cited); [In] = illustrative (a round design parameter that keeps the design's relations; never a measurement of any system); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/B3-the-effect-vocabulary.md (cancellation proof, settle bound, ceiling, settle deadline, forced cleanup 'cancellation stuck', non-proof list, unconditional revocations); B2-state-ownership.md (cleanup failure enters recovery). Bars: length = value x 0.094 px/ms (drawing scale).&#10;[I1] cancel_settle_target_ms_illustrative = 1500 ms. illustrative: design parameter; one target adapter's bound for positive proof that a cancelled primitive is quiet. Must be &lt;= cancel_settle_ceiling_ms_illustrative and &lt; cleanup_ack_timeout_ms_illustrative&#10;[I2] cancel_settle_ceiling_ms_illustrative = 2000 ms. illustrative: design parameter; catalog-wide ceiling pinned in the deployment profile, shared by every target&#10;[I3] cleanup_ack_timeout_ms_illustrative = 10 000 ms. illustrative: design parameter; kernel cleanup acknowledgement deadline. Every settle bound must be strictly shorter" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="650" width="1220" height="111" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="cancel" target="settle"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="settle" target="q1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="yes" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="q1" target="rel1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="600" y="277" /></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="no: the settle&#10;deadline passed" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=9;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;" edge="1" parent="1" source="q1" target="forced"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="600" y="387" /></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="forced" target="q2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge5" value="yes" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="q2" target="rel2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge6" value="no" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;" edge="1" parent="1" source="q2" target="recov"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line0" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="290" y="202" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1230" y="202" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line1" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="290" y="202" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="290" y="207" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line2" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="478" y="202" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="478" y="207" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line3" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="666" y="202" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="666" y="207" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line4" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="854" y="202" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="854" y="207" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line5" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1042" y="202" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1042" y="207" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line6" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1230" y="202" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1230" y="207" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_06_conformance_ladder" name="06-conformance-ladder"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="871" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="Every experience climbs the same ladder, and 'done' must name its milestone: simulation done authorises no physical deployment until the cross-target milestone holds" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="r0" value="1  KERNEL CONFORMANCE SUITE" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="420" width="236" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b0" value="Parameterised over EVERY registered experience, so a new one is covered with no new kernel test. Proves:&#10;- deterministic replay&#10;- safety preemption from every local state&#10;- departure enters common cleanup&#10;- stale session / generation / command / timestamp rejected&#10;- no raw adapter or middleware access&#10;- effect and primitive allowlists; reserved-policy refusal&#10;- materialise before dispatch; cleanup ack before new admission&#10;- back-to-back sessions keep no authority&#10;- bounded timers, queues, retries, diagnostics&#10;- the claim matrix: never two physical actions; audio-out conflict refused; exclusive head refused under gaze; head-defers-to-gaze in BOTH orders&#10;- stuck cancel -&gt; forced cleanup -&gt; recovery&#10;- lease expiry is never quiescence&#10;- readiness fails if the reasoner profile has tools, context, abilities or camera egress (negative test)&#10;- a gesture from a non-participant track is rejected (negative test)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="70" width="236" height="344" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="r1" value="2  EXPERIENCE SUITE" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="276" y="374" width="236" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b1" value="Written per experience (by the authoring agent if agent-authored, and reviewed with the code):&#10;- transition-matrix tests&#10;- policy validation tests&#10;- happy-path and bounded-failure replay scenarios&#10;- capability-degradation scenarios&#10;- expected command and cancellation traces&#10;- projection tests&#10;&#10;Scenarios read as given / when / then (BDD): given a state and an input, when the event is admitted, then these effects and this evidence." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="276" y="200" width="236" height="168" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="r2" value="3  PLATFORM DEFINITION OF DONE" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="522" y="328" width="236" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b2" value="Milestone criteria that name NO legacy experience. All three contract kinds added through the catalog and invoked through success, cancellation and failure by a purpose-built contract-smoke experience; one new input added through the catalog; the first-registry experiences (greeting, chat, wave, contract smoke) landed through the authoring flow." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="522" y="210" width="236" height="112" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="r3" value="4  SIMULATION ACCEPTANCE" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="768" y="282" width="236" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b3" value="Per experience, on the simulation target; per experience, a clean second browser session back to back with the first." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="768" y="224" width="236" height="52" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="r4" value="5  PHYSICAL ACCEPTANCE" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1014" y="236" width="236" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="b4" value="Hardware-in-the-loop on the robot; sign-off by the architecture and quality reviewers. Agent authorship does not change this gate." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1014" y="178" width="236" height="52" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="m_sim" value="SIMULATION MILESTONE - on the simulation target with no cloud credentials, no network egress, no hardware: rungs 1-4, every safety, authority and cleanup invariant shown by a FAILING negative test, deterministic replay (identical inputs under the replay clock -&gt; identical state encodings, invocation sequences, evidence digests). Showcase artifact: one command -&gt; evidence + a shareable video." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="480" width="974" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="m_chat" value="LIVE-CHAT GATE - the real model, on simulation. A cloud outage may block it, never invalidate the offline milestone." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="768" y="546" width="236" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="m_x" value="CROSS-TARGET MILESTONE - the same experiences pass hardware-in-the-loop with physical adapter and producer contracts AND give equivalent evidence under the cross-target comparator (C3). Until then every profile is simulation-only and physical execution stays disabled." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="612" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="m_note" value="A RICH LEGACY EXPERIENCE IS NOT THE DEFINITION OF DONE: an earlier draft made parity with it the exit criterion and bent the platform toward it. It became a required but non-blocking regeneration experiment (C3)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="546" width="728" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cant" value="WHAT SIMULATION CANNOT PROVE (C1): contact force or hardware safety from simulated grasp; collision truth from browser monocular depth; perception, conversation, social-timing or manipulation quality; a live human run is never a CI test." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1014" y="480" width="236" height="124" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rules" value="EVIDENCE RULES: every invariant needs a negative test that fails when the rule is broken  |  schema-versioned evidence carries the full resource lifecycle of every invocation; comparators READ held intervals from these fields and never infer them from presentation events or terminal outcomes  |  the video illustrates, the evidence proves" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="670" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  rising steps = the ladder, climbed left to right (each rung's box above it says what it proves)  |  amber = kernel-level gates  |  green = per-experience tests  |  blue = simulation  |  purple = live model  |  red = the physical robot and what simulation cannot prove  |  bars below = milestones and the rungs they span." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="726" width="1220" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Mechanisms: this kit's notes/ (named per line below) and glossary.md. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown: [Pn] = public (cited); [In] = illustrative (a round design parameter that keeps the design's relations; never a measurement of any system); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/C2-the-conformance-ladder.md (ladder, kernel conformance list, experience suite, milestones, showcase artifact, live-chat gate, cross-target milestone, platform-native done, evidence rules); C1-simulation-first.md (what simulation cannot prove); C3-regeneration-and-comparison.md (non-blocking regeneration, cross-target comparator). Public: Pact documentation, docs.pact.io (consumer-driven contract tests); North, 'Introducing BDD', 2006 (given / when / then). This page carries no numeric design parameter." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="780" width="1220" height="75" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="r0" target="r1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="r1" target="r2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="r2" target="r3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="r3" target="r4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>